<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec_em-practice" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Practice - Electromagnetism</title>
	
	<!--
	If you want an A*R*C*S (Analyze-Represent-Calculate-Sensemake) activity, use the <project> tag.
	If you want an Explain activity, use the <investigation> tag.
		Use this text for qualitative comparisons: <em>greater than</em>, <em>less than</em>, or <em>equal to</em>
	If you want a Calculate activity, use the <exploration> tag.
	
	<m># \mathrm{~}</m>
	<m> \mathrm{~}</m>
	-->
		
	<subsubsection>
		<title>Numerical Practice</title>
		<activity>
			<title>Wave 1</title>
			<p>
				
			</p>
			<p>
				The electric field of an electromagnetic wave traveling in vacuum is described by the following wave function:
				<md>
					\vec{E} = \left(5.00 \mathrm{~V/m}\right) \cos\left(kx - \left(6.00 \times 10^9 \mathrm{~1/s}\right)t + 0.40\right) \hat{y}
				</md>
			Here, <m>k</m> is the wavenumber, <m>x</m> is in m, and <m>t</m> is in s.  Find the following quantities:
			<ol marker="a.">
				<li>
					<p>
						amplitude
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						frequency
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						wavelength
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						the direction of travel
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						the associated magnetic field
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			</p>
		</activity>
		<activity>
			<title>Wave 2</title>
			<p>
				
			</p>
			<p>
				A plane electromagnetic wave of frequency <m>20 \mathrm{~GHz}</m> moves in the positive <m>y</m>-axis direction such that its electric field is pointed along the <m>z</m>-axis. The amplitude of the electric field is <m>10 \mathrm{~V/m}</m>. The start of time is chosen so that at <m>t=0</m>, the electric field has a value  <m>10 \mathrm{~V/m}</m> at the origin. (a) Write the wave function that will describe the electric field wave. (b) Find the wave function that will describe the associated magnetic field wave.
			</p>
		</activity>
		
	</subsubsection>

<references>
	<biblio xml:id="ref_openstax-em">
